# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_resolve_go_ruby.py" "RESOLVE-GO-RUBY GATE: PASS" "Go pkg-resolution perf index + Ruby bare-require precision guard" "Go package-resolution O(1) index + Ruby bare-require unique-match precision: (1) PERF: _resolve_go_pkg previously did O(go_dirs x imports) linear scan per edge; kubernetes=~183M comparisons=19.6s. Fix: _go_pkg_by_suffix builds a path-segment-suffix index of all Go pkg dirs once; _resolve_go_pkg_indexed uses O(1) dict probes. Semantics and production wiring are byte-proven on mixed local-hit plus high-cardinality external/miss imports, and the release gate deterministically counts the executed production operations: at most one directory-universe build scan, then at least 25x fewer candidate-directory operations than the linear reference, with every live Go edge routed through the indexed helper and none through the linear helper, including misses. Wall-clock remains diagnostic-only because a scheduler pause in the indexed millisecond window made the prior one-shot >=10x ratio flaky on the shared runner. (2) PRECISION: bare single-segment Ruby require 'name' fanned out to ALL local name.rb files; 5188 spurious edges on Rails. Multi-segment requires unaffected. Fix: after family filter, if src is .rb and import is bare single-segment, only accept a UNIQUE local .rb match; suppress ambiguous fan-out. Recall cost near-zero: exactly-one-match still resolves. Content-free: paths and module names only." "Go pkg-resolution perf (deterministic executed-operation + production-wiring proof keeps hit and miss paths on the O(import-depth) index instead of regressing to O(dirs), semantics preserved) and Ruby bare-require precision (unique-match-only guard suppresses ambiguous multi-rb fan-out while leaving unique and multi-segment resolves intact)" 20
